{"candidate_id":"figure-analysis:Figure3:47c82bf2da82fe17","artifact_id":"Figure3","visual_type":"flowchart","description":"This flowchart illustrates the GEPA (Genetic-Pareto) optimization loop. It begins with initialization and enters a loop that continues while a budget is available. The process involves a 'Candidate Pool P' represented as a tree, which is evaluated across tasks in a 'Scores Matrix'. Based on task-specific performance, a 'Filtered Pool (Pareto Frontier)' is created. New candidates are proposed using two strategies: 'Reflective Prompt Mutation' and 'System Aware Merge'. These new candidates are first evaluated on a 'Minibatch M' sampled from 'Dtrain'. If performance improves, the candidate is added to the pool; otherwise, it is discarded.","components":[{"name":"Candidate Pool P","role":"Stores the set of candidate systems being evolved.","visual_evidence":"A box at the top left labeled 'Candidate Pool P' containing a hierarchical tree structure of candidates (P0, P1, P2, P3, P4)."},{"name":"Scores Matrix","role":"Tracks the performance of each candidate on individual tasks.","visual_evidence":"A grid labeled 'Scores Matrix' at the bottom left, showing performance (checkmarks/crosses) for candidates (P0, P1, P2, P4) across different tasks (Task 1, Task 2, Task 3)."},{"name":"Filtered Pool (Pareto Frontier)","role":"Contains non-dominated candidates to ensure diversity and prevent local optima.","visual_evidence":"A box labeled 'Filtered Pool (Pareto Frontier)' at the bottom center, showing a subset of candidates (P1, P2, P3, P4) selected based on the Scores Matrix."},{"name":"Propose New Candidate","role":"The module responsible for generating new candidate systems.","visual_evidence":"A large container on the right labeled 'Propose New Candidate', encompassing two sub-blocks for mutation and merge strategies."},{"name":"Reflective Prompt Mutation","role":"A strategy that uses natural language feedback to update individual prompts.","visual_evidence":"The left sub-block within 'Propose New Candidate' labeled 'Reflective Prompt Mutation', showing steps like 'Reflect and Propose New Prompt'."},{"name":"System Aware Merge","role":"A strategy that combines components from different parent candidates.","visual_evidence":"The right sub-block within 'Propose New Candidate' labeled 'System Aware Merge', showing the combination of modules from different parents."},{"name":"Dtrain","role":"The training dataset used for rollouts and evaluation.","visual_evidence":"A database icon labeled 'Dtrain' in the center, with a dotted line indicating 'Sample' leading to 'Minibatch M'."},{"name":"Minibatch M","role":"A small subset of the training data used for initial, low-cost evaluation of new candidates.","visual_evidence":"A cylinder icon labeled 'Minibatch M' within the 'Propose New Candidate' block."}],"relationships":[{"source_component":"Candidate Pool P","relation":"feeds into","target_component":"Scores Matrix"},{"source_component":"Scores Matrix","relation":"selects best candidates from","target_component":"Filtered Pool (Pareto Frontier)"},{"source_component":"Filtered Pool (Pareto Frontier)","relation":"samples from","target_component":"Propose New Candidate"},{"source_component":"Propose New Candidate","relation":"evaluates on","target_component":"Minibatch M"},{"source_component":"Reflective Prompt Mutation","relation":"is a strategy within","target_component":"Propose New Candidate"},{"source_component":"System Aware Merge","relation":"is a strategy within","target_component":"Propose New Candidate"},{"source_component":"Propose New Candidate","relation":"adds improved candidate to","target_component":"Candidate Pool P"}],"findings":["The GEPA process is a cyclic optimization loop that evolves a pool of candidate AI systems.","Candidates are evaluated task-by-task, and a Pareto-based filtering mechanism is used to select a diverse set of high-performing candidates for further evolution.","New candidates are generated via either Reflective Prompt Mutation or System Aware Merge.","Evaluation is hierarchical: candidates are first tested on a small 'Minibatch M' and only added to the main pool if they show performance improvements."],"citations":[{"section_id":"sec-3","path_id":"3","quote":"Figure 3: GEPA proposes a new candidate in every iteration by improving existing candidates using one of the two strategies"},{"section_id":"sec-3","path_id":"3","quote":"Instead of selecting the best performing candidate to mutate always, which can lead to a local-optimum, GEPA introduces Paretobased candidate sampling"},{"section_id":"sec-3","path_id":"3","quote":"GEPA begins with a candidate pool P containing only the base system, where each candidate is a concrete instantiation"}],"confidence":0.95,"provenance":{"image_sha256":"034b92eef1ddd19bff0ae4ef0a271e94eaf409b203dd0292dd2e251e5f47e1c5","context_sha256":"8419a00cb7cf79fbb2b5e772ee7641dda9c54ebb7d3b970d4c6a7cb0e5b6acde","route_id":"9router-anthropic","protocol":"anthropic_messages","requested_model":"minimax/MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","resolved_model":"mimo-v2.5-free","prompt_sha256":"f60e4aaf9ebeb95130be815cc723bc05b9ed231c85afbe4a3f0c15cc461bf9c2","output_schema_sha256":"a8466bc711b606893973ce728964765ae224e0497a2b92535761e5ef503f2345","input_tokens":6472,"output_tokens":2264,"latency_ms":40662},"authoritative":false,"import_eligible":false}